            <span id="teasertxt">OUT NOW</span>
            <span id="tarrww"><svg id="teaserarrow" viewBox="0 0 100 56" aria-hidden="true"><polygon class="ta-body" points="0,19 52,19 52,4 100,28 52,52 52,37 0,37" /><polygon class="ta-shine" points="6,23 48,23 48,28 6,28" /></svg></span>
            <span id="teasertxt2">!! wow !!</span>
            <span id="teasertxt3">100% free · no virus · trusted&trade;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="win alt resizable" id="win-about" style="left:70px; top:895px; width:340px">
          <div class="win-title"><span class="sq y"></span> ▓ about ▒░</div>
          <p class="small">
            i'm moe p. wellington, a 31-year-old artist from germany. i've been
            working with AI since 2022.
          </p>
          <p class="small">
            my recent work explores the paradox between UI and AI: interfaces
            are systems designed to be read and understood by humans, while AI
            models reconstruct their visual language without understanding the
            logic, intention, or conventions those interfaces were built to
            communicate.
          </p>
          <p class="small">
            what emerges is a kind of false memory of software. worlds that
            appear functional and navigable, but refuse to fully explain
            themselves. this recalls the sensation of encountering videogames
            as a child, before their symbols had settled into meaning: when
            something could feel familiar and operational long before i
            understood how to read it.
          </p>
          <p class="small">
            AI allows me to return to that same condition: a system that seems
            to work, but begins to fall apart the closer you look. information
            before literacy. systems before understanding.
          </p>
